 /*
- * The functions now also return the transaction output data that a
- * TPC-C terminal must display.  Changing the returned columns requires
- * dropping and recreating the functions.
+ * The 0.46 C entry points return the expanded terminal output introduced by
+ * DBT-2 0.62.0.  PostgreSQL cannot replace a function while changing its OUT
+ * row type.  Renaming preserves the old function OID and every dependency;
+ * the old OID is then converted to a SQL compatibility projection, while the
+ * public name is assigned to the expanded C function.
+ *
+ * SQL-standard compatibility bodies are parsed while the extension script
+ * runs, so their calls are bound to the new function OIDs rather than being
+ * resolved through a caller-controlled search_path at execution time.  The
+ * binding also survives ALTER EXTENSION SET SCHEMA.
+ *
+ * This also makes fresh default installation deterministic: dbt2 has no
+ * direct 0.46 base SQL, so CREATE EXTENSION follows this same 0.45--0.46 edge.
  */
 
